 ],
 "literal": "Roaring thunder with, rainy season's beginning united / backyard forest-clearing's jasmine soft vine / teeth-like buds, to the man of such land / sleep abandoned, O friend, my eyes!",
 "translation": "The rainy season has begun, accompanied by roaring thunder. In the forest clearings, the soft vines of the wild jasmine are budding like teeth. For the lord of this land, O friend, my eyes have completely abandoned sleep.",
 "modern": "முழங்குகின்ற இடியோடு கார்காலம் தொடங்கியுள்ளது. கொல்லைப் புறத்துத் தோட்டத்திலுள்ள முல்லையின் மெல்லிய கொடிகள் பற்களைப் போல அரும்புகின்றன. இத்தகைய நாட்டின் தலைவனுக்காக, தோழியே, என் கண்கள் தூக்கத்தைத் துறந்துவிட்டன.",
 "explanation": "The heroine is speaking to her close friend during the rainy season, which belongs to the Mullai landscape. The hero had promised to return before the onset of the rains, but he has not yet arrived. She points out that the rainy season has commenced with roaring thunder, and the wild jasmine vines in the forest clearings are budding. These white buds look like sharp, white teeth, mockingly laughing at her loneliness. Because of her longing for the lord of this land, her eyes have completely lost their sleep. The key words are 'ஆர்கலி' (roaring thunder), 'முல்லை' (wild jasmine), 'எயிறு' (teeth), and 'துயில்' (sleep).",
